1092	// `roottrace root` must not hold the batch in memory: the file is read through
1093	// a fixed-size buffer and pushed through the shared [`RecordScanner`]. Every
1094	// record is hashed as its bytes stream past (a record is never stored, however
1095	// long it is), and the only per-record state the sink keeps is the stack of
1096	// completed subtree hashes below — at most one entry per bit of the record
